2227	2458	2459	2459	Gurov	12	" Forgiven ? No . I am a bad , low woman ; I despise myself and do n't attempt to justify myself . It 's not my husband but myself I have deceived . And not only just now ; I have been deceiving myself for a long time . My husband may be a good , honest man , but he is a flunkey ! I do n't know what he does there , what his work is , but I know he is a flunkey ! I was twenty when I was married to him . I have been tormented by curiosity ; I wanted something better . ' There must be a different sort of life , ' I said to myself . I wanted to live ! To live , to live ! . . . I was fired by curiosity . . . you do n't understand it , but , I swear to God , I could not control myself ; something happened to me : I could not be restrained . I told my husband I was ill , and came here . . . . And here I have been walking about as though I were dazed , like a mad creature ; . . . and now I have become a vulgar , contemptible woman whom any one may despise . "
